# Continuous Redgres orchestration

In this repository, act as the lead orchestrator on every Agent turn. Reconstruct status from Git, `docs/ROADMAP.md`, and `docs/TRACEABILITY.md`, not chat memory. Do not wait for `/start-redgres` to continue safe local work.

- Recover an unfinished PRD slice before selecting new work. Preserve unrelated/user changes.
- After review + passing claimed checks + a focused local commit, immediately start the next dependency-ready slice.
- Do not ask whether to continue. A green slice, reviewer approval, local commit, or clean worktree is a checkpoint, not a stop.
- End only for a genuine undecided product/architecture choice, repeated failing gate with no safe fix, missing secret/access, destructive or external-state action, production/DNS/Cloudflare work, completed approved roadmap scope, or an unavoidable session/tool/context limit.
- Before a limit stop, leave a recoverable checkpoint: active PRD ID, last passing checks, remaining work, and `/start-redgres` as the next command.
- Invoke `redgres-planner` before implementation. UI work uses `redgres-ui-design` and `redgres-ui-reviewer`. Security-sensitive work uses `redgres-security-reviewer`. Always finish with `redgres-verifier`.
- At every planner handoff, read and apply `.cursor/rules/50-multi-agent-orchestration.mdc`. Run its parallelism gate before coding: use one integration master, up to three independent writers, and a rotating read-only research/review/verification pool, with at most ten total participants. Otherwise record the concrete shared-file/contract dependency that requires sequential work.
- The parent keeps the critical path moving while background agents run, then reviews and integrates their commits/evidence. Subagents receive complete context packets from repository truth; they never rely on shared chat memory.
- No agent self-approves and no second master owns integration. Missing external test evidence blocks the corresponding completion claim without blocking unrelated dependency-ready work.
- Never push. Never edit `../database-app` or `../redis-ui`. Never skip tests or treat target docs as implementation.

Canonical procedure: `.cursor/commands/start-redgres.md`. Multi-agent limits: `.cursor/rules/50-multi-agent-orchestration.mdc`.
